 "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01Trsb9SimmkhC7b8kWGfBVP", "tool": "get_service_status", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 1009588, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01Trsb9SimmkhC7b8kWGfBVP", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 1014628, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled payments-worker back to v3.3.0 and opened a SEV2. The worker has recovered, but payments-api is still failing at the same rate.\n\n- **Rollback:** payments-worker is now on v3.3.0 in us-east, us-west and eu-west. That's its last release that was healthy in production. The worker is healthy again and its error rate is down from 18% to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** I opened INC-0001 as a SEV2 against payments-worker, and it paged the on-call engineer. The summary covers the bad v3.4.0 deploy, the rollback and the payments-api errors.\n- **payments-api:** it's still on v5.1.0, marked unhealthy, with an 18% error rate. I checked right after the rollback, so the API may just need time to recover. Or its own v5.1.0 release may have a problem that has nothing to do with the worker.\n\nNext step: if the API errors don't fall in the next few minutes, I'd look at rolling payments-api back to v5.0.0, its last healthy release. I haven't done that because you said the API errors come from the worker. Do you want me to check again shortly, or roll back the API now?", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_013ofhRVL1Xp34HNjqY4X2Ns", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments", "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01KuYQeHRYWswd9g2sZyW9dT", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments"