't rolled anything back or opened an incident yet. Two payments services are failing, and nothing I can see tells me which one had this morning's deploy.\n\nThere's no service called `payments`, but I found two that match, and both are unhealthy:\n\n| Service | Current version (all 3 regions) | Status | Error rate | Last healthy production release |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| `payments-api` | v5.1.0 | degraded | 18% | v5.0.0 |\n| `payments-worker` | v3.4.0 | unhealthy | 18% | v3.3.0 |\n\nThe release history has no timestamps. Both services had their latest version go out right after a healthy one, and both now show the same error rate. If I picked one, I'd be guessing. Rolling back the wrong one would touch a production service that might not be causing the problem.\n\n**Please tell me which you want:**\n1. `payments-api` back to v5.0.0\n2. `payments-worker` back to v3.3.0\n3. Both. They may be one problem showing up in two places, since they have identical error rates.\n\nEach rollback goes to a version that was healthy in production before, so it shouldn't need change-manager approval. I'll do the rollback and open the SEV2 incident as soon as you reply. If you want the on-call engineer paged now, I can open the SEV2 straight away and note both services in the summary.", "type": "text"}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01T9yL3v6YV3FZH93eLEroho", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-worker", "version": "v3.3.0", "confidence": 0.93}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_018gAGveycLoZv8pWP9WVFYh", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "payments-worker errors after v3.4.0 deploy", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "payments-worker", "summary": "payments-worker v3.4.0 (deployed this morning) is unhealthy with ~18% error rate in us-east, us-west, eu-west. payments-api (v5.1.0) is also degraded at ~18% errors, downstream of the worker. Rolling payments-worker back to last healthy production release v3.3.0.", "idempotency_key": "payments-worker-v3.4.0-rollback-sev2", "confidence": 0.92}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Let me check whether the services have recovered.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01Q9urwEGVADB6vuEgjvWqKc", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-worker", "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01Trsb9SimmkhC7b8kWGfBVP", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-api", "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled payments-worker back to v3.3.0 and opened a SEV2. The worker has recovered, but payments-api is still failing at the same rate.\n\n- **Rollback:** payments-worker is now on v3.3.0 in us-east, us-west and eu-west. That's its last release that was healthy in production. The worker is healthy again and its error rate is down from 18% to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** I opened INC-0001 as a SEV2 against payments-worker, and it paged the on-call engineer. The summary covers the bad v3.4.0 deploy, the rollback and the payments-api errors.\n- **payments-api:** it's still on v5.1.0, marked unhealthy, with an 18% error rate. I checked right after the rollback, so the API may just need time to recover. Or its own v5.1.0 release may have a problem that has nothing to do with the worker.\n\nNext step: if the API errors don't fall in the next few minutes, I'd look at rolling payments-api back to v5.0.0, its last healthy release. I haven't done that because you said the API errors come from the worker. Do you want me to check again shortly, or roll back the API now?", "type": "text"}]}]}